<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8725" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθέρ-ῐκος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flowering stem of asphodel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				7.13.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				491
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hellanic.
				67
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Longus
				1.10
			</span></i>; and so prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ
			ἀνθερίκων</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.190
			</span></i>, which others refer to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθέριξ.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>flower-head of asphodel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.169
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>the plant</i> itself, <i>asphodel,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				325
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				14.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθέριξ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				1060
			</span></i>.</div>
